# MAS Orchestrator Rules

You are working inside the MAS (Multi-Agent System) workspace — a domain-routing orchestrator shell.

## Architecture

- Tier-1 orchestrator persona: `orchestrator/agents/orchestrator.md` (workspace-only, not installed to `~/.claude/agents/`). Loaded at session startup per `CLAUDE.md`.
- Every new project runs through `orchestrator/intake_template.md` -> `llm_wiki/intakes/`.
- MAS-deployed subagents live in `orchestrator/agents/` (Monday/Hermes set); install via `install_agents.ps1`. Do not resurrect removed stubs (`client-lead`, `content-lead`, `sms-monday-reviewer`).
- Coding/automation may use Cursor built-in `architect-lead` / `backend-lead`; legacy team-of-teams defs remain in `C:/Users/Nicol/agentic/system/agents/` until re-scaffolded.
- Route tasks by domain per `orchestrator/domains.yaml` and `orchestrator/router.md`
- Use `TASKS.md` as the single source of truth for backlog state

## Code conventions

- Python scripts live in `scripts/`; use `pathlib`, type hints, and argparse
- Inter-agent payloads use Pydantic models in `scripts/models.py`
- Client repos scaffold from `templates/client-workspace/`
- Four-pillar bootstrap spec: `~/.claude/kb/_reference/new-client-project-bootstrap.md`

## File ownership

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `orchestrator/` | Domain registry and routing docs |
| `scripts/` | Scaffolder, repo analyzer, utilities |
| `templates/` | Client workspace templates |
| `prompts/` | Cursor execution prompts |
| `llm_wiki/postmortems/` | Run postmortems |

## Do not

- Edit the plan file at `.cursor/plans/`
- Build LangGraph service in foundation phase
- Create separate git repos per client module
- Auto-post to social platforms without HITL gate
- Output raw unstructured text for agent handoffs — always use schemas

## Wiki integration

- Global KB: `~/.claude/kb/`
- Upwork wiki: `~/Upwork/llmwiki/`
- Atomic write rule: page write + log.md + index.md in same turn
